From d4c5566940d098c745e18e8185e3c7ec4dbd7c37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CIQ Kernel Automation <ciq_kernel_automation@ciq.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:56:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] s390/pkey: Check length in pkey_pckmo handler implementation

jira VULN-194839
cve CVE-2026-64558
commit-author Holger Dengler <dengler@linux.ibm.com>
commit 1ac287e2af9a9112fe271427ef45eceb26bce8b4

Explicitly check the length of the target buffer in the pkey_pckmo
implementation of the key_to_protkey() handler function. The handler
function fails, if the generated output data exceeds the length of the
provided target buffer.

	Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Fixes: 8fcc231ce3be ("s390/pkey: Introduce pkey base with handler registry and handler modules")
	Reported-by: Christian Borntraeger <borntraeger@linux.ibm.com>
	Reviewed-by: Harald Freudenberger <freude@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Holger Dengler <dengler@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Alexander Gordeev <agordeev@linux.ibm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1ac287e2af9a9112fe271427ef45eceb26bce8b4)
	Signed-off-by: CIQ Kernel Automation <ciq_kernel_automation@ciq.com>
---
 drivers/s390/crypto/pkey_pckmo.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/s390/crypto/pkey_pckmo.c b/drivers/s390/crypto/pkey_pckmo.c
index 835d59f4fbc56..1e32cbf6a576c 100644
--- a/drivers/s390/crypto/pkey_pckmo.c
+++ b/drivers/s390/crypto/pkey_pckmo.c
@@ -257,6 +257,10 @@ static int pckmo_key2protkey(const u8 *key, u32 keylen,
 				goto out;
 			break;
 		}
+		if (t->len > *protkeylen) {
+			rc = -EINVAL;
+			goto out;
+		}
 		memcpy(protkey, t->protkey, t->len);
 		*protkeylen = t->len;
 		*protkeytype = t->keytype;
-- 
2.52.0

